meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-cm33-anim
==================================

CM33 boot animation for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. The Cortex-M33 plays an
animation over the still logo of meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still, until the
first Weston frame. The Cortex-A55 only loads the frames in U-Boot; it is not
involved while the animation plays.

Default: a 12-dot spinner below the Renesas wordmark, with a simulated
percentage inside. The percentage counts from 1 % to 99 % in 20 s
(FLA_ANIM_PROGRESS_S), then stays at 99 % while the spinner keeps turning.

Tested with RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, Multi-OS package v4.2.0,
MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", core-image-weston.


I. Changes
==========

  U-Boot    Adds a second display layer over the still logo. Loads the
            animation frames from /boot and passes them to the CM33.
  CM33      Bare-metal firmware, started by BL2. It switches the frames
            until Linux takes over the display. The frames before the loop
            start are played once, the rest loops.
  Frames    Made at build time and installed into /boot: the spinner with
            the percentage, or own PNG files (FLA_ANIM_FRAMES).
  Multi-OS  BL2 loading of the CM33 firmware is enabled.


II. Build
=========

Start from the default BSP build environment (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide,
2.2). Extract the Multi-OS package in the workspace, then add the layers:

  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rz-features/meta-rz-multi-os/meta-rzg/meta-rzg3l
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still
  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-cm33-anim

Set in conf/local.conf:

  USE_OPENAMP = "0"

Build:

  $ MACHINE=smarc-rzg3l bitbake core-image-weston


III. Notes
==========

  - Cannot be combined with meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence.
  - With meta-rzg3l-fast-boot: add meta-rzg3l-fast-boot first.
  - The time from 1 % to 99 %, the frames, the frame time and the position
    are set in local.conf with FLA_ANIM_*. See the guide, section 5.3.
    For example, 99 % after 12 s:

      FLA_ANIM_PROGRESS_S = "12"

  - Every frame is stored. U-Boot loads them after the logo is on screen,
    before the kernel starts: about 0.27 s with the default (172 frames,
    25 MB). A longer FLA_ANIM_PROGRESS_S means more frames and more time.
  - The percentage is simulated. It does not follow the boot progress.
  - OpenAMP cannot be used on the CM33 at the same time.
